From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:07:10 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] raumata: choose a native profile and which protocol owns the
 air

One radio stays on a Meshtastic or MeshCore preset. The operating mode selects that profile, which stack advertises, and how the shared airtime budget is split.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

diff --git a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
index 1ad6969dadb61285d4c0a4cbc7ba97ae88a155e0..667f2f1991b3b345ea950c951e8634b396b9d478 100644
--- a/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
+++ b/docs/raumata-dual-protocol.md
@@ -7,27 +7,45 @@ mesh without a hardware modification.
 ## Shared PHY profiles
 
 A LoRa receiver has one demodulator configuration at a time. Raumata keeps the
-SX1262 in **one selectable physical configuration (`PhyProfile`)** stored in NVS
-(`raumata/phy`) and shared by both stacks:
-
-- **Meshtastic presets** (`ANZ LongFast`, `ANZ MediumSlow`, `ANZ ShortFast`,
-  `US LongFast`, `EU868 LongFast`): native sync word `0x2B`, 16-symbol preamble,
-  region/channel frequency calculation.
-- **MeshCore presets** (`Australia (Narrow)` 916.575 MHz BW62.5/SF7/CR7,
+SX1262 in **one physical configuration** taken from a native preset. An
+operating mode (`raumata/mode`) chooses which family supplies that
+configuration and how the two stacks share the radio:
+
+| Mode | Physical configuration | Who transmits |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `mainly-meshtastic` | Meshtastic preset (sync `0x2B`, 16-symbol preamble) | Meshtastic presence and about 90% of the airtime budget. MeshCore stays available to the companion and does not advertise. |
+| `mainly-meshcore` | MeshCore preset (sync `0x12`, 32-symbol preamble) | MeshCore presence and about 90% of the airtime budget. Meshtastic background traffic (nodeinfo, position, telemetry) stays off; messages the phone sends still go out. |
+| `shared-meshtastic` | Meshtastic preset | Both stacks advertise and send, each with about half of the airtime budget. |
+| `shared-meshcore` | MeshCore preset | Both stacks advertise and send, each with about half of the airtime budget. |
+
+There is no sync word that lets stock Meshtastic peers and stock MeshCore peers
+hear the same transmission. A Meshtastic profile reaches stock Meshtastic
+peers. A MeshCore profile reaches stock MeshCore peers. The other protocol is
+on that same configuration, so its peers must be Raumata nodes or configured to
+match.
+
+Presets:
+
+- **Meshtastic:** `ANZ LongFast`, `ANZ MediumSlow`, `ANZ ShortFast`,
+  `US LongFast`, `EU868 LongFast`.
+- **MeshCore:** `Australia (Narrow)` 916.575 MHz BW62.5/SF7/CR7,
   `New Zealand (Narrow)` 917.375 MHz, `US/Canada (Narrow)` 910.525 MHz,
-  `Portugal 868` 869.618 MHz): native sync word `0x12`, 32-symbol preamble,
-  explicit frequency override.
-- **Dual presets** (`Dual AU (common 0x2B)` and `Dual AU (common 0x12)`):
-  explicit 916.575 MHz BW62.5/SF7/CR7 with a chosen common sync word.
-- **Custom (`255`)**: user-defined frequency, bandwidth, spreading factor,
-  coding rate, sync word, preamble length, and TX power.
-
-`raumata::phyInit()` loads the active profile before `initLoRa()` and drives
+  `Portugal 868` 869.618 MHz.
+
+`raumata::phyInit()` loads the mode and profile before `initLoRa()` and drives
 both `config.lora` and `RadioInterface`'s `syncWord` and `preambleLength`.
-Runtime changes from either the Meshtastic radio configuration or the MeshCore
-companion API (`CMD_SET_RADIO_PARAMS`, `CMD_SET_RADIO_TX_POWER`,
-`CMD_SET_PHY_PROFILE`, or CLI `phy list|get|set`) reconfigure the radio once for
-both stacks and schedule a rate-limited re-advertisement.
+A profile from the other family is rejected. `CMD_SET_RADIO_PARAMS` selects a
+MeshCore preset only when the mode is using a MeshCore profile and the
+frequency, bandwidth, spreading factor, and coding rate match that preset.
+The Meshtastic app can change the preset while the mode uses a Meshtastic
+profile; in a MeshCore-profile mode those edits are put back.
+
+Runtime changes use the companion custom vars `mode` and `phy.id`,
+`CMD_SET_PHY_PROFILE`, or CLI `mode get|list|set` and `phy list|get|set`.
+The radio reconfigures once and schedules a rate-limited re-advertisement for
+whichever stacks the new mode allows to announce themselves. A node with no
+saved mode keeps both stacks on, using a Meshtastic profile unless the saved
+profile was already a MeshCore one.
 
 ## Frame demultiplexing
 
